abstract: >-
  Constructions and arithmetic restrictions for the 3x3 magic square of
  squares through its common-difference transversal frame. Using Aebi's
  primitive-triangle classification, the paper derives uniqueness of a
  positive square progression for each difference with at most three prime
  factors. Using the complete S-unit totals of von Känel and Matschke, it
  excludes full magic for differences supported on primes at most 19,
  classifies 384 primitive nine-square/seven-line arrays modulo grid symmetry
  and square scaling, and determines their sharp difference-normalized
  defect minimum. Two infinite eight-square/seven-line constructions and a
  finite difference-840 bridge classification accompany an integral line-sum
  calculation, fixed-difference interaction and finiteness results, and a
  variable-difference signed-root surface whose associated degree-five
  reconstruction over Q(cone) has generic Galois group S5. The full signed
  cover has degree 40. Fixing the difference requires an additional
  rational-square lift; the Galois-group statement is not asserted for
  that fixed-difference model. Local support laws
  describe an arbitrary four-prime frontier that remains open. Exact Python
  replays cover the elementary and symbolic computations; external-CAS
  records are authenticated and parsed, not independently recomputed.
